 "prompt_sha256": "fb413062632a781b66bbb4a33541d80216a63e737b95431367f69603efcd413a",
 "answer": "To generate embeddings using Ollama, you should call the `/api/embed` endpoint. This endpoint can take input either directly or via a command-line interface (CLI). The input typically consists of text that you wish to convert into embeddings.\n\nHere are the methods and inputs for calling this endpoint:\n\n1. **CLI Method:**\n   - You can run the command directly in the shell:\n     ```shell\n     ollama run embeddinggemma \"Hello world\"\n     ```\n   - Alternatively, you can pipe text to the command:\n     ```shell\n     echo \"Hello world\" | ollama run embeddinggemma\n     ```\n   - The output will be a JSON array containing the embeddings.\n\n2. **cURL Method:**\n   - Use the following cURL command to send a POST request:\n     ```shell\n     curl -X POST http://localhost:11434/api/embed \\\n       -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n       -d '{\n         \"model\": \"embeddinggemma\",\n         \"input\": \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\"\n       }'\n     ```\n\n3. **Python Method:**\n   - You can use the following Python code to generate embeddings:\n     ```python\n     import ollama\n\n     single = ollama.embed(\n       model='embeddinggemma',\n       input='The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.'\n     )\n     print(len(single['embeddings'][0]))  # vector length\n     ```\n\nIn each of these methods, the `input` is the text string you wish to generate embeddings for, and the `model` is specified as `embeddinggemma` or another suitable model from the Ollama library. The result will be a JSON array containing the generated embeddings.",
